Today I solved leetcode question 1807:Evaluate the Bracket Pairs of a String.

Description: We are given a strring and a 2D array.
              In string we are given some keys.
              eg- MyNameIs(name).
              And in array we are given 2 values at each index.
              eg-[["name","Ashish"]]
              So we must change the key inside the string s to the value given in array.
              And if there is no value then we must replace it with a question mark.
              O/P- MyNameIsAshish.
              
Solution: First we must make a hashmap named 'check' to store all the key-value pairs of array.
          Then we create variable named 'ans' to store our final answer.
          Then we will start our loop and we will keep first condition as if(s[i]=='(').
          In this condition we will get what is our key.
          Then we will create a variable named 'key'.
          And we will store all the character till we reach ')'.
          Then we will check whether our hashmap has it's value or not.
          If yes then we will add that value to our 'ans' variable.
          If not the we will add '?' to our 'ans'.
          And if there is no '(' at start we will just add all other characters.
